# Build output.
#
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING. A gitignore pattern with no slash matches at
# every depth and matches directories as readily as files, so an unanchored
# `go-ride-simulator` would also match any directory of that name. Anchored, it
# matches only the binary `go build` drops at the repository root -- which was
# committed, at 6.5MB, because no pattern covered it.
/go-ride-simulator

bin/
*.exe
*.test
.DS_Store
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
